<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis Pasteur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis Pasteur was a nineteenth-century French scientist whose work on microbes, fermentation and vaccines founded modern microbiology. He was among the scientists befriended by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II of Brazil</a>, who took a keen interest in science. This friendship illustrates the learned character of Pedro's rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-pasteur.jpg" alt="Louis Pasteur" width="305" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_Pasteur,_foto_av_Paul_Nadar,_Crisco_edit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
